      </modifiers>
      <rules>
        <rule id="169f06e8-efea-9bb9-1a13" name="Targetting" hidden="false">
          <description>Instead of picking one target for the Stormsword, pick a target for each of its weapons. The co-axial heavy bolter must fire at the same target as the Siege Cannon.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="42360052-bac6-d044-81f3" name="Ordnance" hidden="false">
          <description>The stormsword may fire Ordnance and still fire other weapons. It may fire Ordnance even if it moved.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="a91c2845-24b2-6264-08ce" name="Lumbering Vehicle" hidden="false">
          <description>The stormsword can move up to 6" a turn. It must always move straight ahead, but can pivot by up to 90 degrees at the end of the move.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="05ac09be-11ae-c9be-c027" name="Difficult Terrain" hidden="false">
          <description>The Stormsword can ignore low walls, hedges, bushes and rubble. Going through other difficult terrain they test as normal, but if they roll a 1 they lose D3" of movement, just as if they had suffered an Engines Damaged result, instead of being immobilised.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
