  </sharedSelectionEntryGroups>
  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="6f523a2a-5292-7332-e453" name="Medallion Crimson" hidden="false">
      <description>The first time the bearer is wounded by an attack that causes instant death he takes a single wound instead.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="8ad072e5-c93d-7015-a383" name="Macharian Cross" hidden="false">
      <description>After deployment is complete, but before determining who has first turn, any single infantry squad (including Hardended Veterans, Storm Troopers, Ogryns, Ratlings, Infantry Platoon squads and Armour Fist Squads, but not any vehicles) within 6" of the Officer may be redeployed up to 12, but must abide by all the mission's deployment zones and rules.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="dd968bc5-2bb5-b217-a596" name="Carapace Armor" hidden="false">
      <description>4+ Armour Save</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="9f5e6a3e-758d-af47-f66f" name="Bionics" hidden="false">
      <description>When a model with bionics is killed, instead place it on its side. Roll a D6 at the start of the next turn: on a roll of 6 the model stands back up with 1 wound, but on any other roll it is removed as a casualty.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="3dc16c80-eee8-3fec-93e1" name="Camo-Cloak" hidden="false">
      <description>The unit adds +1 to any cover save already allowed</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="f8029b31-cb40-2179-f969" name="Advisor" hidden="false">
      <description>Commissars, Priests and Sanctioned Psykers are Advisors. For each type of Advisor, one must be assigned to the Command HQ. Any others of that type are then allocated to Platoon HQ squads. If all Command and Platoon HQ squads have an Advisor of that type, then the remainder join infantry squads, armoured first squads or storm trooper squads.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="7e5cff4a-d93d-b437-efa7" name="Vox-Caster" hidden="false">
      <description>If a unit containing an Officer has a vo-xcaster, then one squad per turn that also has a vox-caster may use the Leadership ability of the officer regardless of distance. The benefits of standards and trademark items are not conveyed through the vox-caster</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="c081e107-af3f-67bb-b9ab" name="Master Vox-Caster" hidden="false">
      <description>Any number of squads may use the Leadership of the HQ's Officier for a single Morale or Leadership tests rather than the usual limit of one allowed with a Vox-Caster.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="b8340cc7-7e49-522e-db4b" name="Regimental Standard" hidden="false">
      <description>Add +1 to the combat resolution of any assault that takes place at least within 6" of the regimental standard. A Regimental Standard also counts as a Company Standard.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="a5ac9b3f-787a-1611-8ef9" name="Refractor Field" hidden="false">
      <description>Gain a 5+ invulnerable save</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="6e1a219f-ba3e-48e1-d853" name="Iron Discipline" hidden="false">
      <description>Any unit using the Leadership ability of an Officer or Senior Officer with Iron Discipline ignore the -1 modifier for being under half strength and may regroup even if below half strength.

Incompatible with: Chem-inhalers</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="7a50c323-7535-4e8f-3be8" name="Trademark Item" hidden="false">
      <description>A unit led by a person who carries a trademark item may re-roll any failed Morale or Pinning checks it suffers. However, if the character is slain, the unit must pass a Morale test to avoid falling back.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="d9a988c2-64a7-17f2-60c2" name="It's For Your Own Good!" hidden="false">
      <description>If a Sanctioned Psyker attached to the same unit as a Commissar suffers a Perils of the Warp attack, the Commissar will immediately execute him to prevent him from being possessed. Remove the Psyker as a casualty without triggering the power or the Perils of the Warp.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="818f48b8-a753-adac-8a73" name="Die-hards" hidden="false">
      <description>Do not count negative Moral modifiers for being outnumbered in close combat.

Incompatible with: Chem-inhalers</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="efc2b77d-dd7c-1fd5-20e7" name="Hardened Fighters" hidden="false">
      <description>Gain +1 to WS. Sentinels additionally gain +1 A.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="cf144677-a296-7948-e840" name="Jungle Fighters" hidden="false">
      <description>Gain the following:
- Can see 12" through forest or jungle terrain

- Recieve a 4+ Cover save when in forest or jungle terrain

- Move full speed through forest or jungle terrain

- May infilitrate if the mission permits if they can deploy into forest or jungle terrain

- May include a Heavy Flamer instead of Heavy Weapon, but can never take lascannons

- Reduce armour to 6+</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="f1b74376-1b3d-19c1-d750" name="Close Order Drill" hidden="false">
      <description>If the unit has all units in base to base contact with each other then the models in the unit gain +1 Leadership and +1 Initiative.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="fa530722-b646-5bfc-6244" name="Light Infantry" hidden="false">
      <description>Any unit without a Chimera:
- Rolls 2D6 and take the highest for moving through difficult terrain

- May infilitrate

- May take a sniper rifle instead of a heavy weapon</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="e8046603-f233-df9e-91ea" name="Sharpshooters" hidden="false">
      <description>Any Guard infantry model with a BS 3 may re-roll to hit rolls of 1. May not be used on Plasma weapons or Sniper Rifles.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1f4f4a6a-676b-922b-42f9" name="Xeno-Fighters" hidden="false">
      <description>Xeno-fighters hit on a 3+ regardless of respoective Weapon Skill values against their preferred enemy. This advantage does not apply against Independent Characters, Tyranid Monstrous Creatures, or Monstrous Creatures.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="2e27823e-bdaf-1619-7f8e" name="Chem-inhaler" hidden="false">
      <description>The unit will always test Morale, Leadership or Pinning with no negative modifiers. If they fail a Morale check for 25% shooting casualties, they will be pinned rather than fall back.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="f5841b1b-9e5c-5727-8dfe" name="Cameleonline" hidden="false">
      <description>The unit adds +1 to any cover save already allowed</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="28991007-2e34-a447-0495" name="Cyber-Enhancement" hidden="false">
      <description>Gain invulnerable save of 6+</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="c533f59e-0b5c-fdef-023f" name="Warrior Weapons" hidden="false">
      <description>Replace lasguns with laspistols and close combat weapons</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1bfa7bde-7132-d658-b484" name="Telepathic Order" hidden="false">
      <description>The Psyker extends the zone of influence of an Officer he is accompanying. Use at the start of the Imperial Guard turn. If the test is passed, the Leadership radius of the Officer in the same squad as the Psyker is extended to 18" until the start of the next Imperial Guard turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="2223113b-e466-80b0-ef34" name="Psychic Ward" hidden="false">
      <description>If a psychic power would normally affect the Sanctioned Psyker or the unit he is accompanying, make a Psychic test. If the test is passed then roll a D6. On a 4+ the power is cancelled.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="eb752819-5424-da58-2311" name="Psychic Lash" hidden="false">
      <description>Make a Psychic test at the start of the Imperial Guard Assault phase. If successful, the power remains in phase until the start of the next Imperial Guard Assault phase. Thje Psyker's may choose to use the Lash in place of its normal attacks. The Psyker gets D3 Attacks (with no bonuses) at Strength 3, with any wounds ignoring Armour saves.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="8caff530-052c-c87c-fc56" name="Machine Curse" hidden="false">
      <description>Make the Psychic test at the start of the Assault phase. If passed the power is effective until the end of the same Assault phase. Make one close combat attack against a vehicle in base contact with the Psyker. If a hit is scored, roll a D6:
1 - 3: No effect
4 - 5: Inflict Glancing Hit
6 : Inflict Penetrating Hit</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="bd9d8c78-3ff3-c010-80fc" name="Amphibious" hidden="false">
      <description>Treat all water features as clear terrain when moving</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="4cdce786-2156-4953-ac50" name="Improved Comms" hidden="false">
      <description>The Imperial Guard player may re-roll one Reserves roll per turn, adn to re-roll the dice when checking to see if an enemy unit or obstacle is hit by a preliminary bombardment</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="de29c25a-7eb5-a73a-136f" name="Immobile" hidden="false">
      <description>Once deployed, the model may not be moved unless towed.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="856d81db-adc7-df7d-4fa7" name="Anti-Air" hidden="false">
      <description>Roll to hit aircraft using the firers normal BS</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="55ed53d8-f96f-1e0f-9c9c" name="VTOL Hover Mode" hidden="false">
      <description>Rather than leave the table as per normal, the flyer may choose to engage is VTOL Hover mode to remain on the table. It remains stationary, but can turn in any direction to bring its weapons to bear. It may fire all of its weapons.
For the purposes of being fired at, the vehicle counts as a moving Skimmer. It can therefore be fired at using the firer's normal BS. All hits are treated as glancing hits. It can only be attack in close combat by attackers that can fly or have jump packs, in which case it is treated as a moving vehicle.
If the vehicle is immobilised the model is destroyed.
At the end of its own turn, the vehicle may disengage VTOL. It not reverts to being a flyer. It cannot return in the enemy turn immediately afer it leaves the table.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="d8370eec-a4a2-414a-f414" name="Searchlight" hidden="false">
      <description>During Night Fighting missions, one enemy unit spotted by the vehicle can be fired at by any other Imperial Guard units in range and with line of fire. However, the vehicle using the Searchlight will then be exposed and can be fired at by any enemy units that are in range and line of sight of it until the next turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="a7190b04-4b7a-ae72-439b" name="Smoke Launchers" hidden="false">
      <description>Once per game, after completing movement, a vehicle with smoke launchers may trigger them. The vehicle cannot fire and use its smoke launchers in the same turn. Any penetrating hits scored by the enemy in the next Shooting phase count as glancing hits.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="68bf2609-cb35-4b8a-113b" name="Medi-pack" hidden="false">
      <description>Medi-packs allow a unit with a medic to ignore the first failed saving throw it rolls in every turn. The medi-pack may not be used on any model which suffers instant death or that has been hit by a close combat weapon that allows no Amrour save. It may not be used if the medic is in base contact with an enemy model.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="c62be228-9059-53b7-e494" name="Leadership" hidden="false">
      <description>Any Imperial Guard squad within 12" of the officer may use his Leadership value for all Morale and Pinning tests.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="42e7d15b-82ba-ff94-d4f2" name="Armoured Crew Compartment" hidden="false">
      <description>The vehicle no longer counts as being open-topped.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="7e925068-9d4b-fc0d-2c15" name="Camo Netting" hidden="false">
      <description>In scenarios using the Hidden Set-up rules, vehicles carrying camo netting can be set up hidden anywhere in their deployment zone.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="a53e4444-7755-6a09-59d1" name="Extra Armour" hidden="false">
      <description>Count the 'Crew Stunned' result as 'Crew Shaken' instead</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="eab00017-7fc2-f36c-76fb" name="Mine Sweeper" hidden="false">
      <description>The vehicle may enter a minefield without being attack. Any minefield the vehicle moves across is cleared and removed from play</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="4f4a89a3-bd55-bee6-59ce" name="Rough Terrain Modification" hidden="false">
      <description>A vehicle that moves no more than 6" may re-rolled failed Difficult Terrain tests</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="75902bce-e846-9d55-8362" name="Track Guards" hidden="false">
      <description>The vehicle treats 'Immobilised' results as 'Crew Stunned' on a roll of a 4+. This does not combine with the extra armour ability.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="a2c4ab24-c987-57ca-5d74" name="Company Standard" hidden="false">
      <description>Units of Imperial Guard Infantry with a model within 12" of the standard can re-roll failed Morale tests.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="e8a31e75-52c4-07e8-9424" name="Holy Relic" hidden="false">
      <description>Once per battle. On any turn the model with the relic does not move they may reveal it. All friendly models that are within 2D6" gain +1 Attacks for the rest of that turn. The relic may be revealed in the opposing player's turn assuming the model with the relic did not move in the previous turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="f1847e62-88eb-8f02-360f" name="Honorifica Imperialis" hidden="false">
      <description>The wearer gains the stats of a Heroic Senior Officer, but does not become an officer or an independent character</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="6f148006-d094-d68a-e7e1" name="Master-crafted Weapons" hidden="false">
      <description>The bearer may re-roll one failed to hit roll per turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="a5e8b9fb-4b91-7898-c587" name="Purity Seals" hidden="false">
      <description>If a model wearing seals falls back, roll one extra D6 for Fall Back distance, and then discard the dice of your choice. If the model is part of a unit this ability applies to the whole unit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="ec190424-70a5-bc0c-078f" name="Rosarius" hidden="false">
      <description>Gain a 4+ Invulnerable save.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="ef632985-e63e-464d-07f7" name="Signum" hidden="false">
      <description>Once per turn, re-roll one missed to hit shooting roll for the Techpriest or one of his attendant Servitors</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="423a9e2f-8534-f254-5fe8" name="Surveyor" hidden="false">
      <description>If enemy infiltrators set up with 4D6" of a model with a surveyor then the model is allowed to take a 'free' shot at them. If the model is part of a unit, the whole unit may shoot. These shots are taken before the battle begins and may cause the infiltrators to fall back.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Drop Troops" id="18603af7-6034-8744-c246" hidden="false">
      <description>Any Infantry units or Sentinels may Deep Strike if the mission permits.

Incompatible with Warrior Weapons</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Grenadiers" id="891d6aaf-71cd-1ca9-9787" hidden="false">
      <description>0-3 Storm Trooper squads can be taken as Troops, but can't Deep Strike or Infiltrate

Incompatible with: Warrior Weapons</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Mechanised" id="cee496ee-15e4-9cbf-4e95" hidden="false">
      <description>All Infantry units must take a Chimera transport


Incompatible with: Warrior Weapons, Light Infantry</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Independent Commissars" id="8fa7c4cb-b699-8dee-b3b3" hidden="false">
      <description>A squad of 1-3 Commissars may be taken as an Elite choice</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Veterans" id="9cdb7b52-2e89-7c0f-3f8b" hidden="false">
      <description>Exempt from standard 0-1 limit on Hardened Veterans</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Priests" id="a1143175-ed2c-ede4-0759" hidden="false">
      <description>Allows the use of Priests</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Techpriest Enginseers" id="df31d627-5327-ac28-4cb0" hidden="false">
      <description>Allows the use of Techpriest Enginseers</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Sanctioned Psykers" id="b9f1fd31-5d56-5bab-9ee7" hidden="false">
      <description>Allows the use of Sanctioned Psykers</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ratling Squads" id="2249f844-3c4b-1183-4ed2" hidden="false">
      <description>Allows the use of Ratling Squads</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ogryn Squads" id="02489b7f-eaa7-3f71-27e8" hidden="false">
      <description>Allows the use of Ogryn Squads</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Special Weapon Squads" id="8da48da5-384b-18b3-86b1" hidden="false">
      <description>Allows the use of Special Weapon Squads</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Conscript Platoons" id="595f5863-19e0-e8c5-c5b4" hidden="false">
      <description>Allows the use of Conscript Platoons</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Rough Rider Squadrons" id="aaae102e-45c8-b80a-037c" hidden="false">
      <description>Allows the use of Rough Rider Squadrons</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Heavy Weapon Platoons" id="e78b4933-a130-72d9-756d" hidden="false">
      <description>Allows the use of Heavy Weapon Platoons</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Storm Trooper Squads" id="6bd19e90-665a-e1f7-c917" hidden="false">
      <description>Allows the use of Storm Trooper Squads</description>
    </rule>
    <rule xmlns="http://www.battlescribe.net/schema/gameSystemSchema" id="0d2520d3-1fb8-c8fc-9a48" name="Smoke &amp; Blind Grenades" hidden="false">
      <description>One use only.

Blind/smoke grenades are used in the Shooting phase instead of the unit firing any weapons. Mark the unit as using its blind/smoke grenades by placing cotton wool around them. A unit cannot assault on the same turn it uses blind/smoke grenades. The blind/smoke screen lasts until the start of the player's next turn and until then the unit counts as in cover with a 5+ cover save. Because they count as being in cover, models in the unit will also strike first if assaulting, unless the enemy is armed with something like frag grenades, or has an ability that allows them to always strike first.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule xmlns="http://www.battlescribe.net/schema/gameSystemSchema" id="44260ec4-ae2f-c1b3-1094" name="Deathwatch" hidden="false">
      <description>Deathwatch squad members and characters are never subject to the Special rules which apply to specific Chapters (i.e. Space Wolves' counter attack, Blood Angels' Black Rage, Black Templars' vows, etc.) and which affect their fighting abilities or battlefield behaviour. Must be equipped with bolters or combi-weapons.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule xmlns="http://www.battlescribe.net/schema/gameSystemSchema" id="889df47f-a4ad-1300-b80f" name="Flyers" hidden="false">
      <description>-Starts in reserve and moves only in a straight line


-Roll a die for them each turn starting with the 2nd round, as usual for a reserve unit


-Place on any table edge facing the desired direction. Cannot shoot or be shot at until it makes it's attack run


-Move flyer to desired distance following the opponent's Movement Phase but before their shooting phase


-Attacks following the opponent's shooting phase


-Can pivot up to 45 degrees before or after making it's attack (but not both) unless Shaken or Stunned


-Can fire all weapons regardless of distance moved


-Can make further attack runs on rolls of +2


TARGETING FLYERS:


-Attacker cannot use Ordnance or Barrage weapons


-Add 12" to range measurement


-Hits only on a roll of 6


-All successful hits are glancing. 


-Stunned and shaken results prevent Flyer from attacking. Immobilized results destroy the Flyer</description>
    </rule>
    <rule xmlns="http://www.battlescribe.net/schema/gameSystemSchema" id="4d265bbf-068f-ddcd-9c4c" name="Super-Heavy Flyer" hidden="false">
      <description>-Moves up to 6" per turn but can pivot up to 90 degrees at the end of a move


-May fire Ordnance and still fire other weapons. Can also fire Ordnance after moving.


-Can shoot more than one target if desired, picking a target for each weapon.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule xmlns="http://www.battlescribe.net/schema/gameSystemSchema" id="a92fa602-0ca0-3d4e-9193" name="Titan Killer" hidden="false"/>
    <rule xmlns="http://www.battlescribe.net/schema/gameSystemSchema" id="464a74f0-ad48-7817-0d08" name="Fast" hidden="false">
      <description>-Can move up to 24" in Movement Phase


-Can fire all weapons when moved up to 6"


-Can fire one weapon when moved up to 12"


-Cannot fire any weapons when moved more than 12"</description>
    </rule>
    <rule xmlns="http://www.battlescribe.net/schema/gameSystemSchema" id="d193063a-258d-e801-482f" name="Storm Shield" hidden="false">
      <description>Allows a 4+ invulnerable save against one opponent per turn in close combat. Cannot be combined with Rosarius or Iron Halo saves</description>
    </rule>
    <rule xmlns="http://www.battlescribe.net/schema/gameSystemSchema" id="57ae44c5-9cec-9031-2fd0" name="Combi Weapons" hidden="false" publicationId="e621-2cd6-fe95-920f" page="34">
      <description>These are basically two weapons joined together, giving the wielder a choice of two weapons to fire instead of one. A wielder who is armed with a combi-weapon may choose which of the weapons it is going to use in the shooting phase. The regular weapon may be fired any number of times. but the other weapon may only be fired once per battle. Note that you may not choose to fire both weapons at once.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
